1
00:00:04,318 --> 00:00:09,558
With my head full of George Barnwell, I was at first disposed to believe that I must have had

2
00:00:09,559 --> 00:00:15,199
some hand in the attack upon my sister, or at all events that as her near relation, popularly

3
00:00:15,199 --> 00:00:21,959
known to be under obligations to her, I was a more legitimate object of suspicion than any one else.

4
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:27,600
But when, in the clearer light of next morning, I began to reconsider the matter and to hear it

5
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:35,040
discussed around me on all sides, I took another view of the case, which was more reasonable.

6
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:40,719
Joe had been at the Three Jolly Bargemen, smoking his pipe, from a quarter after eight o’clock to a

7
00:00:40,719 --> 00:00:46,559
quarter before ten. While he was there, my sister had been seen standing at the kitchen door,

8
00:00:46,559 --> 00:00:52,398
and had exchanged Good Night with a farm-labourer going home. The man could not be more particular

9
00:00:52,398 --> 00:00:57,558
as to the time at which he saw her (he got into dense confusion when he tried to be),

10
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:04,559
than that it must have been before nine. When Joe went home at five minutes before ten, he found her

11
00:01:04,559 --> 00:01:10,559
struck down on the floor, and promptly called in assistance. The fire had not then burnt unusually

12
00:01:10,559 --> 00:01:17,639
low, nor was the snuff of the candle very long; the candle, however, had been blown out.

13
00:01:17,639 --> 00:01:22,760
Nothing had been taken away from any part of the house. Neither, beyond the blowing out of

14
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:28,238
the candle,—which stood on a table between the door and my sister, and was behind her when she

15
00:01:28,238 --> 00:01:33,238
stood facing the fire and was struck,—was there any disarrangement of the kitchen,

16
00:01:33,238 --> 00:01:39,158
excepting such as she herself had made, in falling and bleeding. But, there was one

17
00:01:39,158 --> 00:01:45,279
remarkable piece of evidence on the spot. She had been struck with something blunt and heavy,

18
00:01:45,279 --> 00:01:50,799
on the head and spine; after the blows were dealt, something heavy had been thrown down

19
00:01:50,799 --> 00:01:57,398
at her with considerable violence, as she lay on her face. And on the ground beside her,

20
00:01:57,398 --> 00:02:04,318
when Joe picked her up, was a convict’s leg-iron which had been filed asunder.

21
00:02:04,318 --> 00:02:10,840
Now, Joe, examining this iron with a smith’s eye, declared it to have been filed asunder some time

22
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:17,279
ago. The hue and cry going off to the Hulks, and people coming thence to examine the iron,

23
00:02:17,279 --> 00:02:22,279
Joe’s opinion was corroborated. They did not undertake to say when it had left the

24
00:02:22,279 --> 00:02:27,398
prison-ships to which it undoubtedly had once belonged; but they claimed to know for certain

25
00:02:27,398 --> 00:02:32,238
that that particular manacle had not been worn by either of the two convicts who had escaped

26
00:02:32,238 --> 00:02:39,439
last night. Further, one of those two was already retaken, and had not freed himself of his iron.

27
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:42,959
Knowing what I knew, I set up an inference of my own here.

28
00:02:43,879 --> 00:02:50,760
I believed the iron to be my convict’s iron,—the iron I had seen and heard him filing at,

29
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:58,318
on the marshes,—but my mind did not accuse him of having put it to its latest use. For

30
00:02:58,318 --> 00:03:03,519
I believed one of two other persons to have become possessed of it, and to have turned

31
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:10,959
it to this cruel account. Either Orlick, or the strange man who had shown me the file.

32
00:03:10,959 --> 00:03:17,920
Now, as to Orlick; he had gone to town exactly as he told us when we picked him up at the turnpike,

33
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:22,959
he had been seen about town all the evening, he had been in divers companies in several

34
00:03:22,959 --> 00:03:29,639
public-houses, and he had come back with myself and Mr. Wopsle. There was nothing against him,

35
00:03:29,639 --> 00:03:35,799
save the quarrel; and my sister had quarrelled with him, and with everybody else about her,

36
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:43,040
ten thousand times. As to the strange man; if he had come back for his two bank-notes

37
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:47,199
there could have been no dispute about them, because my sister was fully prepared

38
00:03:47,199 --> 00:03:52,959
to restore them. Besides, there had been no altercation; the assailant had come

39
00:03:52,959 --> 00:03:58,199
in so silently and suddenly, that she had been felled before she could look round.

40
00:03:58,199 --> 00:04:04,359
It was horrible to think that I had provided the weapon, however undesignedly, but I could hardly

41
00:04:04,359 --> 00:04:10,879
think otherwise. I suffered unspeakable trouble while I considered and reconsidered whether I

42
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:18,318
should at last dissolve that spell of my childhood and tell Joe all the story. For months afterwards,

43
00:04:18,318 --> 00:04:24,000
I every day settled the question finally in the negative, and reopened and reargued it

44
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:31,279
next morning. The contention came, after all, to this;—the secret was such an old one now,

45
00:04:31,279 --> 00:04:38,279
had so grown into me and become a part of myself, that I could not tear it away. In addition to the

46
00:04:38,279 --> 00:04:43,599
dread that, having led up to so much mischief, it would be now more likely than ever to alienate

47
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:50,040
Joe from me if he believed it, I had a further restraining dread that he would not believe it,

48
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:58,040
but would assort it with the fabulous dogs and veal-cutlets as a monstrous invention. However,

49
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:03,318
I temporized with myself, of course—for, was I not wavering between right and wrong,

50
00:05:03,318 --> 00:05:08,599
when the thing is always done?—and resolved to make a full disclosure if I should see

51
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:12,840
any such new occasion as a new chance of helping in the discovery of the assailant.

52
00:05:14,158 --> 00:05:19,079
The Constables and the Bow Street men from London—for, this happened in the days of

53
00:05:19,079 --> 00:05:24,840
the extinct red-waistcoated police—were about the house for a week or two, and did pretty much what

54
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:30,680
I have heard and read of like authorities doing in other such cases. They took up several obviously

55
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:36,438
wrong people, and they ran their heads very hard against wrong ideas, and persisted in trying to

56
00:05:36,438 --> 00:05:42,878
fit the circumstances to the ideas, instead of trying to extract ideas from the circumstances.

57
00:05:42,879 --> 00:05:47,638
Also, they stood about the door of the Jolly Bargemen, with knowing and reserved looks that

58
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:52,520
filled the whole neighbourhood with admiration; and they had a mysterious manner of taking their

59
00:05:52,520 --> 00:06:00,561
drink, that was almost as good as taking the culprit. But not quite, for they never did it.

60
00:06:00,561 --> 00:06:05,240
Long after these constitutional powers had dispersed, my sister lay very ill in

61
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:12,840
bed. Her sight was disturbed, so that she saw objects multiplied, and grasped at visionary

62
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:19,798
teacups and wineglasses instead of the realities; her hearing was greatly impaired; her memory also;

63
00:06:19,798 --> 00:06:27,359
and her speech was unintelligible. When, at last, she came round so far as to be helped downstairs,

64
00:06:27,359 --> 00:06:32,598
it was still necessary to keep my slate always by her, that she might indicate in writing what she

65
00:06:32,599 --> 00:06:39,240
could not indicate in speech. As she was (very bad handwriting apart) a more than indifferent

66
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:45,159
speller, and as Joe was a more than indifferent reader, extraordinary complications arose between

67
00:06:45,159 --> 00:06:51,879
them which I was always called in to solve. The administration of mutton instead of medicine,

68
00:06:51,879 --> 00:06:59,520
the substitution of Tea for Joe, and the baker for bacon, were among the mildest of my own mistakes.

69
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:06,599
However, her temper was greatly improved, and she was patient. A tremulous uncertainty of the action

70
00:07:06,599 --> 00:07:12,638
of all her limbs soon became a part of her regular state, and afterwards, at intervals of two or

71
00:07:12,638 --> 00:07:19,039
three months, she would often put her hands to her head, and would then remain for about a week at a

72
00:07:19,039 --> 00:07:27,599
time in some gloomy aberration of mind. We were at a loss to find a suitable attendant for her, until

73
00:07:27,599 --> 00:07:35,080
a circumstance happened conveniently to relieve us. Mr. Wopsle’s great-aunt conquered a confirmed

74
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:41,919
habit of living into which she had fallen, and Biddy became a part of our establishment.

75
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:45,719
It may have been about a month after my sister’s reappearance in the kitchen,

76
00:07:45,719 --> 00:07:51,000
when Biddy came to us with a small speckled box containing the whole of her worldly effects,

77
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:56,561
and became a blessing to the household. Above all, she was a blessing to Joe,

78
00:07:56,561 --> 00:08:02,000
for the dear old fellow was sadly cut up by the constant contemplation of the wreck of his wife,

79
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:07,118
and had been accustomed, while attending on her of an evening, to turn to me every now and then

80
00:08:07,118 --> 00:08:13,199
and say, with his blue eyes moistened, “Such a fine figure of a woman as she once were,

81
00:08:13,199 --> 00:08:19,719
Pip!” Biddy instantly taking the cleverest charge of her as though she had studied her from infancy;

82
00:08:19,719 --> 00:08:24,680
Joe became able in some sort to appreciate the greater quiet of his life, and to get down to

83
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:30,561
the Jolly Bargemen now and then for a change that did him good. It was characteristic of the police

84
00:08:30,561 --> 00:08:36,400
people that they had all more or less suspected poor Joe (though he never knew it), and that they

85
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:42,919
had to a man concurred in regarding him as one of the deepest spirits they had ever encountered.

86
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:47,599
Biddy’s first triumph in her new office, was to solve a difficulty that had completely

87
00:08:47,599 --> 00:08:54,759
vanquished me. I had tried hard at it, but had made nothing of it. Thus it was:—

88
00:08:54,759 --> 00:08:59,798
Again and again and again, my sister had traced upon the slate, a character that looked like a

89
00:08:59,798 --> 00:09:05,400
curious T, and then with the utmost eagerness had called our attention to it as something

90
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:11,319
she particularly wanted. I had in vain tried everything producible that began with a T,

91
00:09:11,319 --> 00:09:17,840
from tar to toast and tub. At length it had come into my head that the sign looked like a hammer,

92
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:23,438
and on my lustily calling that word in my sister’s ear, she had begun to hammer on the table and had

93
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:30,679
expressed a qualified assent. Thereupon, I had brought in all our hammers, one after another,

94
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:36,798
but without avail. Then I bethought me of a crutch, the shape being much the same,

95
00:09:36,798 --> 00:09:42,520
and I borrowed one in the village, and displayed it to my sister with considerable confidence.

96
00:09:43,199 --> 00:09:47,039
But she shook her head to that extent when she was shown it,

97
00:09:47,039 --> 00:09:53,798
that we were terrified lest in her weak and shattered state she should dislocate her neck.

98
00:09:53,798 --> 00:09:57,319
When my sister found that Biddy was very quick to understand her,

99
00:09:57,319 --> 00:10:02,718
this mysterious sign reappeared on the slate. Biddy looked thoughtfully at it,

100
00:10:02,719 --> 00:10:09,118
heard my explanation, looked thoughtfully at my sister, looked thoughtfully at Joe (who was always

101
00:10:09,118 --> 00:10:15,319
represented on the slate by his initial letter), and ran into the forge, followed by Joe and me.

102
00:10:15,319 --> 00:10:22,000
“Why, of course!” cried Biddy, with an exultant face. “Don’t you see? It’s him!”

103
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:29,199
Orlick, without a doubt! She had lost his name, and could only signify him by his hammer. We

104
00:10:29,199 --> 00:10:33,919
told him why we wanted him to come into the kitchen, and he slowly laid down his hammer,

105
00:10:33,919 --> 00:10:39,438
wiped his brow with his arm, took another wipe at it with his apron, and came slouching out,

106
00:10:39,438 --> 00:10:45,080
with a curious loose vagabond bend in the knees that strongly distinguished him.

107
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:49,479
I confess that I expected to see my sister denounce him, and that I was disappointed

108
00:10:49,479 --> 00:10:55,560
by the different result. She manifested the greatest anxiety to be on good terms with him,

109
00:10:55,561 --> 00:11:00,319
was evidently much pleased by his being at length produced, and motioned that she would

110
00:11:00,319 --> 00:11:05,919
have him given something to drink. She watched his countenance as if she were particularly wishful to

111
00:11:05,919 --> 00:11:12,000
be assured that he took kindly to his reception, she showed every possible desire to conciliate

112
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,278
him, and there was an air of humble propitiation in all she did, such as I have seen pervade the

113
00:11:18,278 --> 00:11:25,438
bearing of a child towards a hard master. After that day, a day rarely passed without her drawing

114
00:11:25,438 --> 00:11:31,958
the hammer on her slate, and without Orlick’s slouching in and standing doggedly before her, as

115
00:11:31,958 --> 00:11:34,991
if he knew no more than I did what to make of it. Chapter 17.
